---
id: org.dxos.spec.deus
name: Deus
version: 0.1.0
---

The spec for `@dxos/deus` itself: the tooling around the `.mdl` language. The language is defined
in `lang/` and motivated in `docs/DESIGN.md`. This document covers what the package must do, so far
only for the spec changelog.

## Extensions

| Term       | URI                          |
| ---------- | ---------------------------- |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`      |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`  |

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Attributed decision log
  A spec carries a `## Changelog` of `decision` blocks (`lang/changelog.mdl`) that traces how it
  came to say what it says, with decisions made by people kept apart from decisions made by agents.

  req F-1.1: Each decision names exactly one decider in `by:`, typed `user:<handle>` (GitHub username or email) or `agent:<name>`.
  req F-1.2: An agent is named by its harness, never by the model that served it.
  req F-1.3: An `agent:` decision names the person it acted for in `for:`; a `user:` decision has no `for:`.
  req F-1.4: A `user:` decision may carry the person's words verbatim in `quote:`; an `agent:` decision may not.
  req F-1.5: The log is append-only. A reversal is a new decision with `supersedes: D-n`.
  req F-1.6: Decision ids are `D-1`, `D-2`, … in the order appended, newest last.
  req F-1.7: Approval of agent decisions is a new `user:` decision whose prose says what it approves.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Every spec change adds a decision
  req F-2.1: A change to a spec outside `## Changelog` adds at least one new decision.
  req F-2.2: A new spec starts with at least one decision.
  req F-2.3: `scripts/check-changelog.ts` enforces F-1.5, F-1.6, F-2.1 and F-2.2 by comparing each changed `.mdl` file with the merge base, and runs in CI as "Check spec changelogs".
  req F-2.4: Language definitions (`lang/`), review rules (`rules/`) and test fixtures are not specs and are exempt.
  req F-2.5: Only `decision` blocks under `## Changelog` form the log; examples elsewhere are ignored.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Linting
  req F-3.1: The editor linter and `scripts/lint-mdl.ts` report decisions that break F-1.1, F-1.3 or F-1.4.
  req F-3.2: `lint-mdl.ts --only <source>` restricts output to one check, so the block-type check (which knows only built-in types) does not hide decision errors.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Agent guidance
  req F-4.1: The repo has an `mdl` skill (`.agents/skills/mdl/SKILL.md`) for writing specs and recording decisions.
  req F-4.2: The skill tells an agent to record a person's input first, faithfully — adding context, never assumptions — and its own additions as separate decisions.
```

## Changelog

Backfilled on 2026-10-20 from the session that built the changelog,
https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093.

```mdl
decision D-1: Specs have a changelog of authoritative decisions, each tagged with the person (username or email) or agent that made it, to trace how decisions were made and separate people from agents.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  quote: |
    I wanna add a changelog section to mdl specs
    the sections has a log of authoritative decisions -- each one is tagged by person (username/email) or agent that made it
    the goal is to trace how decissions were made and separate people and agents
  affects: [F-1]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The repo has an mdl skill.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  quote: ensure there's an mdl skill in the repo
  affects: [F-4.1]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The changelog is a `decision` block type in a new dialect, `lang/changelog.mdl`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: Every other construct in the language is an `ext`-defined block in a dialect file; a dialect keeps the changelog opt-in per document.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A decider is `user:<handle>` or `agent:<name>`, and an agent is named by its harness, not its model. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2]
  why: A typed prefix makes "which decisions did a person make" a filter, and the linter can reject untyped entries. Models change mid-session; the name must stay stable across the log.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: An agent decision names the person it acted for in `for:`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3]
  why: An agent decides within latitude a person gave it; the trace is incomplete without whose.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The log is append-only with monotonic `D-n` ids; reversals use `supersedes:`. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.5, F-1.6]
  why: An edited entry erases the trace the log exists to keep.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A person endorsing an agent decision is recorded as `ratified-by:` on that entry, the only edit an entry admits. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Only decisions that change what the spec requires are logged; edits, renames and reformatting are not. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: Read from "authoritative decisions" in [D-1]; git already records edits.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Decision attribution is linted in the editor and by `scripts/lint-mdl.ts`, whose `--only` flag isolates one check.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3]
  why: The existing block-type check knows only built-in types and flags valid dialect blocks, so a CLI without a filter is unusable on real specs.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Specs are written by people and agents together; each source of knowledge gets its own decision. The agent first records the person's input faithfully, adding only context and no assumptions, then records its own additions as separate decisions. A person approving an agent's design is its own decision.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  quote: |
    Specs are usually collab between humans and agent, the human gives coarse ideas and agent fills in the gaps. its important that the knowledge is separated in different decision entries.

    The agent first records faithful representation of what human wrote, only adding context, no assumptions. and then it could add its own edits as a separate decision.

    person aprooving agent design is its own deicision as well.

    1. put that into skill
  affects: [F-1.7, F-4.2]
  supersedes: D-7
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Every change to a spec adds a decision, and this is enforced mechanically.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  quote: |
    2. all changes to spec must add a decision
    3. lets see how we can enforce (2) mechanically
  affects: [F-2]
  supersedes: D-8
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Approval is not a separate kind of entry; it is an ordinary decision whose prose says what it approves.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  quote: they are the same entry -- approval is not entry kind, could be just a prose
  context: Said in response to a proposed `approves:` field for approval entries, which was dropped before it landed.
  affects: [F-1.7]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14093
```

```mdl
decision D-13: A `user:` decision may carry `quote:` (verbatim words) and `context:` (added facts); an agent decision may not carry `quote:`. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: Separate fields keep the person's words apart from what the recording agent added, so "faithful" can be checked by reading.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: `scripts/check-changelog.ts` enforces [D-11] in CI by diffing each changed `.mdl` against the merge base, and also rejects edited, removed, reordered or out-of-sequence entries. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3]
  why: A diff against the base is the only place "this change added no decision" is visible; the same diff checks append-only for free. Placed beside the changesets check, which works the same way.
  rejected:
    - A Claude Stop hook alone: only covers agent sessions on the Claude harness, not human edits or other harnesses.
    - A husky pre-commit hook: skippable, and not run in the cloud sandbox.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Language definitions, review rules and test fixtures are exempt from [D-11], and only decisions under `## Changelog` count as the log. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.4, F-2.5]
  why: These `.mdl` files are not specs of a component; `lang/changelog.mdl` itself shows example decisions that must not be read as its log.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Deus has a spec of its own, backfilled from the session that built the changelog.
  date: 2026-10-20
